{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile record_pass/_pass_is_due: either read the written epoch content or document that only st_mtime is authoritative (and consider writing empty).","criteria":["maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["src/rebar/_snapshot/gc_trigger.py:89: `fh.write(str(int(time.time())))`","src/rebar/_snapshot/gc_trigger.py:103: `age = time.time() - os.stat(_stamp_path(root)).st_mtime`"],"finding":"record_pass writes the current epoch as the stamp file's CONTENTS, but _pass_is_due decides staleness solely from os.stat().st_mtime and never reads the file body. The written integer is dead data — any reader that trusted the content (e.g. a future operator/debug tool) would find it, but the module's own liveness logic ignores it, so the two can silently diverge (e.g. a touched-but-not-rewritten file).","id":"0","impact":0.3,"location":"src/rebar/_snapshot/gc_trigger.py:84","norm_id":"n87a75dd3432c2ed3","priority":0.2571,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":true,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Avoid the per-call mkdir on the quiet decision path (stat the stamp directly / create the gc dir lazily only when writing), or soften the 'one stat' claim in code/docs.","criteria":["maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["src/rebar/_snapshot/gc_trigger.py:67-68: `d = root / \"gc\"` then `d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)`","src/rebar/_snapshot/gc_trigger.py:94-106: `_pass_is_due` calls `os.stat(_stamp_path(root))` which routes through `_gc_dir`","docs/adr/0005-snapshot-cache-architecture.md amendment: \"the in-line cost is one marker `stat`\""],"finding":"maybe_gc's quiet-path decision is documented as 'one O(1) stat' / 'the whole point', but _pass_is_due -> _stamp_path -> _gc_dir calls d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True) on every invocation, so each gate op incurs a mkdir syscall (and directory creation on first run) in addition to the stat. This contradicts the ADR/docs 'the in-line cost is one marker stat'.","id":"1","impact":0.3,"location":"src/rebar/_snapshot/gc_trigger.py:65","norm_id":"ncc75af80df298409","priority":0.2571,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":true,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"common","unversioned_published_contract_break":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.5,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Close the parent's log_fh after Popen (in a finally) so the parent does not leak an fd per detached GC spawn.","criteria":["error-handling","maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["src/rebar/_snapshot/gc_trigger.py:196: `log_fh = open(_log_path(root), \"a\")  # noqa: SIM115 — handed to the child`","src/rebar/_snapshot/gc_trigger.py:200-217: `subprocess.Popen(... stderr=log_fh, ...)` with no subsequent `log_fh.close()`","ABSENCE: no close of log_fh anywhere in _spawn_detached_gc (mirrors the same pattern in compact_trigger._spawn_detached_sweep)"],"finding":"In _spawn_detached_gc the parent opens log_fh = open(_log_path(root), 'a') and hands it to the child via stderr=log_fh, but never closes the parent's copy of that file descriptor. After Popen dups it into the child, the parent's fd leaks for the lifetime of the process (repeated across gate ops on a long-lived embedding host).","id":"2","impact":0.0,"location":"src/rebar/_snapshot/gc_trigger